  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Westminster Foundation for Democracy. Inclusive Policy Initiative - Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Inclusive Policy Initiative (IPI) will work with Members of Parliament (MPs), women, girls, Persons with Disabilities (PWDs), key marginalised populations and partners to give voice and create space for policy and legislative debate on how to mitigate the impact of discriminatory and punitive policies on vulnerable and marginalised groups and to better protect their rights. Critically, the project and its interventions are designed to complement and build on progress achieved under Westminster Foundation for Democracy&apos;s (WFD) Global Equality Project (GEP), funded by the FCDO. Larger and more connected coalitions will be better able to engage on human rights issues with policy and law makers, targeting policy and legislation related to gender and sexual rights.</narrative>
  </description>
